# Copy to .env, in this directory. Everything is optional.
#
# Two kinds of line. A few are for the host and docker compose, read before the node starts.
# Every other KEY=value line is a setting of the node: bin/up pushes it once the node answers
# (bin/push-settings), and the node keeps it in data/state/settings.json. The node's own
# settings, with their defaults, are listed below and in the dashboard's Settings view (or
# GET /api/settings); any other name is kept as a value of your own, for whatever needs it.
# bin/up only ever sets: to remove a setting for good, clear it in the dashboard (or
# DELETE /api/settings/NAME) and take its line out of this file.
#
# Agents need a provider: OpenRouter, with the key below, or a ChatGPT subscription for models
# openai-codex/<model>, connected from the dashboard (see README). Either, or both.

## For the host and compose; the defaults are shown.
# NANO_CHECKOUT=../nano-checkout   (the clone of this repo mounted at /app; agents can rewrite it)
# NODE_COOKIE=                     (random, generated when the image is built)
# STATE_DIR=/data/state            (agents' saved state, the settings, the ChatGPT tokens; ./data/state on the host)
# SPILL_DIR=/data/spill

## Settings of the node.
# A dedicated OpenRouter key with a low spending limit: every agent can read it.
# Without it, OpenRouter is off and agents on its models are refused (or halted, if it is cleared).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional; the defaults are shown. Each agent's model, reasoning level and limits are not set
# here: they are given whenever an agent is started, and have no defaults.
# NODE_MAX_TOKENS_PER_HOUR=100000000   (across all agents; 0 = no limit)
# EVAL_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# MAX_BINDINGS_BYTES=16000000
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# CHATGPT_BASE_URL=https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex
# CHATGPT_AUTH_URL=https://auth.openai.com
# CHATGPT_CLIENT_VERSION=0.160.1   (models are listed for clients this new; keep at Codex's latest release)
# Stated in each agent's system prompt, so agents started earlier keep the value they started with:
# SYSTEM_PROMPT_FILE=priv/system_prompt.txt
# RESULT_MAX_BYTES=51200
# NETWORK_POLICY=unrestricted outbound internet access   (change it only when you change the network)

## Values of your own, for whatever needs them, such as a key for a search service:
# EXA_API_KEY=
